OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,FHe said plumes of gas "a few tens of
OL,7,Fkilometres in size" and lasting
OL,8,Fbetween five and ten minutes after
OL,9,Fimpact, were observed by the Very
OL,10,FLarge Telescope in Chile, which is
OL,11,Foperated by the European Southern
OL,12,FObservatory.
OL,14,FAlthough this shows evidence of the
OL,15,Faccidental collision, it could be
OL,16,Fseveral days before high-resolution
OL,17,Fimages can be obtained from lunar
OL,18,Fsatellites.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
