OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,FThe second part served as the
OL,7,Fworkhorse to propel the robotic
OL,8,Flanders on their path to the moon.
OL,9,FAfter its mission was complete, this
OL,10,Fstage remained in space and was left
OL,11,Fto orbit the earth.
OL,13,F"Essentially a mixture of solar
OL,14,Factivity and gravity forces have put
OL,15,Fit on a path toward the moon,"
OL,16,FJulianna Scheiman, SpaceX director of
OL,17,FNasa science and Dragon programs, said
OL,18,Fon Monday.
OL,20,FWithout fuel, the rocket could not be
OL,21,Fcontrolled, nor its course be altered.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/17
