OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,FHowever, despite tens of thousands of
OL,7,Fpieces of space junk orbiting the
OL,8,FEarth, incidences of man-made objects
OL,9,Fcrashing into the moon are relatively
OL,10,Frare.
OL,12,FDuring the 20th century space race,
OL,13,Fboth US and Soviet spacecraft crashed
OL,14,Finto the moon. However, many of these
OL,15,Fincidents were intentional tests or
OL,16,Fdeliberate mission endings.
OL,18,FIn 2022, a discarded Chinese rocket
OL,19,Fstage collided with the moon following
OL,20,Fa lunar test mission in 2014.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
