PN,31709
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,FThe rocket was expected to hit the
OL,7,Fsurface of the moon at 5,400mph,
OL,8,Flikely leaving behind a crater with a
OL,9,Fdiameter of approximately 65 to 90
OL,10,Ffeet (20 to 30 meters) on the moon's
OL,11,Fsurface, according to a preprint study
OL,12,Fauthored by a group of scientists,
OL,13,Fincluding researchers at Nasa.
OL,15,FScientists are still analysing and
OL,16,Fmapping data about the collision.
OL,18,FHow could an incident like this affect
OL,19,Fthe future of space travel?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
