FL,318,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31710
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,FThe US space agency is planning to
OL,7,Fcreate a more sustained human presence
OL,8,Fon the lunar surface through the
OL,9,FArtemis programme.
OL,11,FBut if there are plans for missions to
OL,12,Fcreate industry, settlement or further
OL,13,Fresearch on the Moon, greater
OL,14,Fregulation is needed to prevent a
OL,15,Frepeat of the crash, Professor Hugh
OL,16,FLewis, a space safety expert at the
OL,17,FUniversity of Birmingham, said.
OL,19,F"It speaks to an issue that is already
OL,20,Fthere and is going to be getting worse
OL,21,Fin the future," he said.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31711
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,F"If the Moon becomes a true
OL,7,Fdestination for us, with settlements,
OL,8,Fpotentially industry, then that's
OL,9,Fgoing to require orbital
OL,10,Finfrastructure, lots of missions from
OL,11,FEarth to the moon.
OL,13,F"We could see these kinds of events
OL,14,Fhappening again in the future, then
OL,15,Fthey would potentially be posing risks
OL,16,Fto human life, to infrastructure
OL,17,Fthat's there, to science.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31712
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,F"If we're increasing the population of
OL,7,Fspacecraft between the Earth and the
OL,8,FMoon, then you end up with a chance of
OL,9,Fcollision as well, in orbit."
OL,11,FMore events like this could also
OL,12,Fjeopardise the ability to land on
OL,13,Fmoon's surface or potentially
OL,14,Findustrialise, Professor Lewis said.
OL,16,F"SpaceX have been doing a tremendous
OL,17,Fjob of aiming to behave responsibly in
OL,18,FEarth orbit, they are responding to
OL,19,Fregulators," he said.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G12/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31713
SC,0013
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,F"But the real question is whether
OL,7,Fregulation needs to tighten, if we
OL,8,Fneed new standards and guidelines to
OL,9,Fhelp us with missions that go to the
OL,10,Fmoon.
OL,12,F"I know that the Inter-Agency Space
OL,13,FDebris Co-ordination Committee are
OL,14,Fstarting to look at this as a problem,
OL,15,Fand some guidelines about what to do
OL,16,Fwith spacecraft after it has finished
OL,17,Fits mission so that it doesn't pose a
OL,18,Frisk either to the surface or a
OL,19,Fcollision risk around the moon."
OL,21,FWhat can scientists learn from this?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G13/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31714
SC,0014
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,FScientists can use this rare
OL,7,Foccurrence of an artificial object
OL,8,Fhitting the moon to learn more about
OL,9,FEarth's natural satellite - as well as
OL,10,Fprepare for how to shield astronauts
OL,11,Fand any future infrastructure sent
OL,12,Fthere.
OL,14,FProf Lewis said that the consequences
OL,15,Fof the crash represent an exciting
OL,16,Fresearch opportunity.
OL,18,F"That's a surface that has been
OL,19,Fpristine for a very, very long time so
OL,20,Fthere's a lot that could learn by
OL,21,Flooking at the surface," he said.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G14/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31715
SC,0015
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,F"The impact will throw up a lot of
OL,7,Fmaterial and so you could use this as
OL,8,Fan experiment to gain some
OL,9,Funderstanding of learning materials in
OL,10,Fthat particular location."
OL,12,FNasa have also said that scientists
OL,13,Fare "planning to collect lunar data
OL,14,Ffrom the event" in order to "refine
OL,15,Ftechniques for tracking objects in
OL,16,Fspace".
OL,18,FSubscribe for free to our weekly
OL,19,Fnewsletter for exclusive and original
OL,20,Fcoverage from ITV News. Direct to your
OL,21,Finbox every Friday morning.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G15/17
