FL,318,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31716
SC,0016
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786020504
OL,3,CWhat can scientists learn from SpaceX
OL,4,Crocket crashing into the moon?
OL,6,FThere is currently no formalised
OL,7,Ftracking of debris that exists beyond
OL,8,Four planet. Rather, surveys searching
OL,9,Ffor potentially hazardous asteroids
OL,10,Fidentify pieces of space junk that can
OL,11,Fthen be tracked.
OL,13,FSince it's difficult to track and spot
OL,14,Fobjects that slam into the moon, a
OL,15,Fknown event like the upper stage
OL,16,Fcollision helps scientists gain
OL,17,Finsights into properties of the lunar
OL,18,Fsurface, Dr Paul Wiegert, a professor
OL,19,Fof astronomy and physics at the
OL,20,FWestern University in London, noted.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G16/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
